# Dienogest + 10 MeOH: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# Analogous to Dienogest/DMSO/Dienogest_10DMSO_MD.inp and
# Dienogest/DMF/Dienogest_10DMF_MD.inp.
#
# DIFFERENCE FROM THE EARLIER DMSO/DMF BUILDS: this one uses the
# r2SCAN-3c-level gas-phase optimized Dienogest geometry
# (Dienogest/Gas/DienogestGasOptFreq.xyz, converged, r2SCAN-3c TightSCF Opt
# Freq) as the starting structure, rather than the XTB2-level geometry used
# for the earlier DMSO/DMF Explicit10 builds.
#
# Dienogest (r2SCAN-3c) centroid = (-5.521, 1.467, -0.724); max
#   atom-centroid distance = 6.24 Ang (essentially the same size as the
#   XTB2-level geometry used before).
# 10 MeOH molecules, each placed with its O atom (H-bond donor/acceptor
#   site) on the same 12-direction sphere-shell pattern used throughout this
#   project, rotated so the molecule's bulk points radially outward, at
#   offset 10.0 Ang from Dienogest's centroid (same offset used for the
#   DMSO/DMF builds). The MeOH internal geometry itself is also r2SCAN-3c
#   level (from MeOH/Monomer.xyz, r2SCAN-3c/SMD(methanol)-optimized,
#   converged, no imaginary frequency) - the same monomer geometry used
#   throughout this project for MeOH, not an XTB2 geometry.
# Cell Sphere radius set to 15.0 Ang, centered on this structure's own
#   Dienogest centroid.
# Checked: min MeOH-Dienogest atom distance = 3.90 Ang (no clash), max atom
#   distance from the sphere center = 11.92 Ang (safely inside the 15.0 Ang
#   sphere). Total atom count = 108 (48 + 10x6), verified.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere -5.521, 1.467, -0.724, 15.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Dienogest_10MeOH_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

* xyz 0 1
